   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to authorize the town of Irondequoit, in the county of Monroe, to lease parklands to T-Mobile Northeast LLC as successor in interest to Omnipoint Communications Incorporated",
    "basePrintNo": "S7874",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7874-2015",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Parks",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S7874\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to authorize the town of Irondequoit, in the\ncounty of Monroe, to lease parklands to T-Mobile Northeast LLC as\nsuccessor in interest to Omnipoint Communications Incorporated\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nAuthorizes the town of Irondequoit, Monroe County, to lease certain\nparklands to T-Mobile Northeast LLC for the purpose of a wireless\ncommunications facility.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1. Provides the town of Irondequoit governing body with the\nauthority to lease certain parklands to T-Mobile Northeast LLC for a\nperiod not to exceed twenty-six (26) years, at fair market value and\nupon such other terms, conditions and provisions as it deems proper.\nIt also authorizes the granting over parkland for access to the leased\npremises.\n\nSection 2. Validates past actions taken in regards to leasing the\nlands without prior legislative approval.\n\nSection 3. Requires the town of Irondequoit use all revenues received\nfrom any duly enacted lease of parkland to T-Mobile LLC for the\nacquisition of additional parkland and/or for capital improvements of\nexisting park and recreational facilities.\n\nSection 4. Provides description of parklands to be leased to T-Mobile\nNortheast LLC.\n\nSection 5. Provides description of the easement to be granted to\nT-Mobile for access to the leased premises.\n\nSection 6. Provides that should the lands described in sections 4 and\n5 cease to be used for the purposes described in section one of this\nact, the lease shall terminate and those lands shall revert to the\ntown of Irondequoit for public park and recreational purposes.\n\nSection 7. Provides that if the park land that is the subject of this\nact has received federal land and water conservation funding, that\nIrondequoit comply with federal requirements pertaining to the\nconversion of park lands.\n\nSection 8. Effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nIn 2002, the town of lrondequoit executed a lease with Omnipoint\nCommunications, Inc. the use of town-owned parklands for the\ninstallation, use and maintenance of a wireless communications\nfacility. The town failed to secure state legislative approval\nauthorizing, the predecessor in interest of T-Mobile Northeast LLC.\nThis bill would validate that lease and authorize the town to\nnegotiate an additional lease term not to exceed twenty-six years.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone to the State.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
